breadpaper always builds bread-theme with its `extract` feature enabled
(palette extraction from an image is breadpaper's whole purpose), which
statically links bread-palette-extract: a Rust port of code from
ImageMagick and libjpeg-turbo/IJG. That ported code keeps their own licence
terms, reproduced in full in LICENSE-ImageMagick and LICENSE-libjpeg-turbo
(also printed by `breadpaper notice`), and copied here from
bread-palette-extract's own NOTICE/LICENSE-* files (Breadway/bread-ecosystem)
so this binary carries its own copy.

ImageMagick
-----------
Ported: MagickCore/geometry.c (ParseMetaGeometry), resize.c (ResizeImage,
AcquireResizeFilter, SincFast, CubicBC, HorizontalFilter, VerticalFilter),
quantize.c (QuantizeImage, ClassifyImageColors, ReduceImageColors, Reduce,
PruneChild, PruneLevel, PruneToCubeDepth, DefineImageColormap, ClosestColor,
Riemersma/RiemersmaDither, SetGrayscaleImage's gray transform),
histogram.c (UniqueImageColors), color.c (GetColorTuple), and the Q16 HDRI
quantum helpers in quantum.h/pixel-accessor.h, translated from C to Rust.

